Subject: [PATCH 0815/3799] soh: rename func_80078E34 ->
 HealthMeter_StepDisplayedTowardHealth

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: raises the interface's animated health by 0x10 (one sixteenth-heart unit) per call until it reaches gSaveContext.health, returning 1 once it arrives. Unused, but the arithmetic is unambiguous.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c b/soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c
index 9d28860ea..bd8c13218 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c
@@ -291,7 +291,8 @@ s32 HealthMeter_SetHealthToDisplayed(PlayState* play) {
     return 1;
 }
 
-s32 func_80078E34(PlayState* play) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80078E34: raises the interface's animated health by 0x10 (one sixteenth-heart unit) per call until it reaches gSaveContext.health, returning 1 once it arrives. Unused, but the arithmetic is unambiguous.
+s32 HealthMeter_StepDisplayedTowardHealth(PlayState* play) {
     InterfaceContext* interfaceCtx = &play->interfaceCtx;
 
     interfaceCtx->unk_228 = 0x140;
